[
    {
        "id": "sitl04-tab",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "SITL 04 Mode tables",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Set flight modes on ArduPilot and PX4 from each profile's mode table. ArduCopter GUIDED=4 vs PX4 encoded main/sub-mode bitfield \u2014 never cross-use mode numbers.",
        "env": []
    },
    {
        "id": "sitl04-comment",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sitl04-tab",
        "name": "DO_SET_MODE per stack (ArduPilot small int vs PX4 bitfield)",
        "info": "ArduPilot sysid 1: set_mode GUIDED with params {\"1\":1,\"2\":4} (custom_mode 4).\nPX4 sysid 11: set_mode POSCTL using the profile mode table \u2014 custom_mode is an encoded bitfield (example 196608 = POSCTL on many builds), NOT ArduPilot's 4.\n\nLaunch ArduPilot:\n  sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter --out=udp:127.0.0.1:14550\nLaunch PX4 (ports version-specific; verify your build):\n  make px4_sitl gazebo\n  # set MAV_SYS_ID=11; point PX4 Connection at your GCS port (often 14550 broadcast or 14570/14580)\n\nArduPilot Connection: bind 0.0.0.0:14550 \u2192 remote 127.0.0.1:14551.\nPX4 Connection: bind 0.0.0.0:14560 \u2192 remote 127.0.0.1:14561.",
        "x": 300,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
